preConditionHook:
// SHRINKING STAIRS (T00-17, the glossary entry; T26-04 absorbed). Each
// successive new extreme extends LESS than the one before it -- waning
// momentum, and Brooks's warning against the next with-trend breakout.
//
// SIDES. The LONG side reads the BULL extremes -- the swing HIGHS, exactly as
// the merged pseudocode spells it -- and the SHORT side the bear extremes,
// the swing LOWS. So each side reads the series belonging to the trend that
// side would trade WITH, which is what makes the rule usable the way Brooks
// states it: place it NEGATED beside StairsPattern to demand that the bull
// stairs are not yet shrinking before a with-trend long. Taken un-negated it
// is the warning itself.
//
// shrinkLegs is the number of LEGS (gaps between successive pivots), so the
// default 3 means three gaps over FOUR pivots and shrinkLegs - 1 = TWO
// comparisons -- exactly the merged pseudocode, (hi1-hi2) < (hi2-hi3) <
// (hi3-hi4). It is clamped so that needPiv = shrinkLegs + 1 lands in 3..4;
// four pivot slots per series are carried, which is what the default needs.
//
// pivotLookback(50) was added -- the merged parameters omitted the window,
// which is EL's Length and bounds how old the FOURTH pivot may be. It is
// wider than StairsPattern's 40 for exactly that reason: this rule needs one
// more pivot of one series.
//
// THE GAPS ARE NOT REQUIRED TO BE POSITIVE. The merged pseudocode has no such
// term, and adding one would restate StairsPattern's higher-highs test inside
// this rule. A stairs trend is what supplies it; AND the two in a pane. That
// separation is deliberate (a stairs trend can have growing, equal or
// shrinking steps, and only the shrinking case carries the warning) and is
// why StairsPattern is not inlined here despite depends_on_keys naming it.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED rather than calling SwingHigh / SwingLow at
// Occurrence 1..4. The register's swinghigh and swinglow rows are VERIFIED
// but list Occurrence 3+ explicitly as UNMEASURED, and this rule needs a
// fourth. Slice B01 blocked it on that; the inlined scan is the route
// ratified for a third or later pivot, since plain EL loops and comparisons
// are registered and the scan reproduces the MEASURED pivot test exactly
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min):
//
//   * the pivot bar is AT OR ABOVE the pivotStrength OLDER bars and STRICTLY
//     ABOVE the pivotStrength NEWER bars, so a flat top yields exactly ONE
//     pivot, the LATER of the equal bars. Bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER
//     index the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the k < j loop (el_gt) and
//     the at-or-above half the k > j loop (el_ge);
//   * the confirmation lag is exactly pivotStrength bars -- the scan starts
//     at j = pivotStrength and that lag is what makes it lookahead-safe;
//   * candidate offsets run 0 .. Length - 1 from the current bar INCLUSIVE,
//     so j stops at pivotLookback - 1, while the neighbourhood test reaches
//     pivotStrength bars PAST the window: deepest bar touched is
//     pivotLookback - 1 + pivotStrength;
//   * scanning newest-first and recording the first four hits reproduces
//     Occurrence 1, 2, 3, 4;
//   * the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance, hence el_gt /
//     el_ge / el_lt / el_le rather than raw > and >=;
//   * the prices start at the -1 SENTINEL and every gap is gated on the count
//     reaching needPiv -- -1 as a PRICE sits under every real price;
//   * the low side's TIE sense is the mirror of the measured high-side rule
//     rather than an observation, as the swinglow row records.
//
// No WFSafe_SwingHigh exists in MultiWalk, so plain EL governs. Written
// without an early break, matching the EL twin statement for statement:
// Break is not a registered word, so the loops run to the end and the `< 4`
// guards stop a fifth pivot being recorded.
//
// No scratch is declared at hook scope -- every value below is a
// localVariables entry -- because this rule may be placed twice in one
// strategy and its hooks emitted twice into the one class.
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
hiPx4 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
loPx4 = -1.0;
for (int j = (int)pivotStrength; j <= (int)pivotLookback - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - (int)pivotStrength; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + (int)pivotStrength; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 4) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) hiPx1 = high[j];
        if (nHiPiv == 2) hiPx2 = high[j];
        if (nHiPiv == 3) hiPx3 = high[j];
        if (nHiPiv == 4) hiPx4 = high[j];
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 4) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) loPx1 = low[j];
        if (nLoPiv == 2) loPx2 = low[j];
        if (nLoPiv == 3) loPx3 = low[j];
        if (nLoPiv == 4) loPx4 = low[j];
    }
}
needPiv = (int)shrinkLegs + 1;
if (needPiv > 4) needPiv = 4;
if (needPiv < 3) needPiv = 3;
upG1 = hiPx1 - hiPx2;
upG2 = hiPx2 - hiPx3;
upG3 = hiPx3 - hiPx4;
dnG1 = loPx2 - loPx1;
dnG2 = loPx3 - loPx2;
dnG3 = loPx4 - loPx3;
shrinkUp = (nHiPiv >= needPiv);
shrinkDn = (nLoPiv >= needPiv);
if (!el_lt(upG1, upG2)) shrinkUp = false;
if (!el_lt(dnG1, dnG2)) shrinkDn = false;
if (needPiv >= 4) {
    if (!el_lt(upG2, upG3)) shrinkUp = false;
    if (!el_lt(dnG2, dnG3)) shrinkDn = false;
}
